        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">🚗</span> Getting There
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• Cheaha and the Talladega National Forest are east of Birmingham via I-20 and then state highways into the forest; Monte Sano is north via I-65 to Huntsville</li>
              <li>• Cheaha State Park and Monte Sano State Park have their own hours and fees — check each park's official site for current rules</li>
              <li>• Download offline maps; cell service drops in the national forest</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">🎒</span> What to Bring
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• Sturdy shoes — rocky ridge trails and creek crossings are slick when wet</li>
              <li>• Water and food for a longer day than you planned</li>
              <li>• Layers and a rain shell — afternoon storms can build fast in summer</li>
              <li>• Headlamp and a first aid kit</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">📅</span> Best Times to Visit
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• <strong>Summer (Jun-Aug):</strong> Hot and humid with afternoon thunderstorms — start early and carry extra water</li>
              <li>• <strong>Fall (Oct-Nov):</strong> Cooler, drier and clear, the most comfortable season for the ridge routes</li>
              <li>• <strong>Winter (Dec-Feb):</strong> Mild, with leaf-off ridge views; occasional ice on higher ground</li>
              <li>• <strong>Spring (Mar-May):</strong> Wildflowers and high water at creek crossings after heavy rain</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">⚠️</span> Safety First
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-stone-700">
              <li>• Check the forecast and trail conditions before leaving</li>
              <li>• Tell someone your hiking plans</li>
              <li>• Turn back if weather deteriorates</li>
              <li>• Stay on marked trails and be aware of hunting seasons in the national forest — wear blaze orange if you hike then</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
